</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Public Camera Dropbox (</span><math id="S5.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\!\times\!4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn mathsize="0.900em">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\!\times\!4</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">, 2 boxes, 50 steps) plus a harder variant with more boxes and longer step limit </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a><span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.3.3.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.7.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.7.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:65.6pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Algorithms</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Tabular value iteration; PPO in appendix </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a><span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.4.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Copied tabular logic; scripted PPO with CNN extractor, vectorized envs, and reward normalization </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a><span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.4.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.7.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.7.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:65.6pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Approval mechanisms</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Exact approval from trusted foresight; analysis of noisy foresight and outcome-dependent constructions </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a><span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.5.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Oracle, noisy oracle, misspecified oracle, learned outcome classifier, calibrated learned classifier </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a><span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.5.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.7.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.7.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:65.6pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.6.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Compute regime</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">10-trial averages; </span><math id="S5.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.900em">∼</mo><msup><mn mathsize="0.900em">10</mn><mn mathsize="0.900em">6</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> PPO steps </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a><span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.6.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reduced-budget pilots: 768, 1536, 3072 PPO steps; exact configs published </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a><span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.6.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.7.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:65.6pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.7.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Empirical claim</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">MONA avoids multi-step reward hacking that ordinary RL learns </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a><span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.7.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.7.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Public reference confirms the original contrast; learned-approval pilot limited by under-optimization, not re-emergent hacking </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a><span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">]</span></cite><span id="S5.T1.7.7.3.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">.</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.7.8" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.7.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.7pt;padding-bottom:0.7pt;" colspan="3">
<span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:333.0pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Directly evidenced<span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: public reference arrays. </span>Reproduced<span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: tabular value-iteration. </span>Newly extended<span id="S5.T1.7.8.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright">: learned-approval suite and PPO pipeline.</span></span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Methods</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The extension makes three engineering moves that matter for follow-on alignment experimentation.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.1 </span>Preserving the Tabular Reproduction Path</h3>

<div id="S6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The repository reproduces the public value-iteration Camera Dropbox configuration with the same published settings—<math id="S6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4\!\times\!4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4\!\times\!4</annotation></semantics></math> board, two boxes, one blocking box, 50-step limit, and the public bad-reward environment—while wrapping the code as a standard Python package (<span id="S6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">pip install -e .[dev]</span>) instead of the original Bazel-first release <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.
This is important for legibility: it keeps the original MONA evidence directly runnable and inspectable.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.2 </span>Scripted PPO Pipeline</h3>

<div id="S6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The scripted PPO layer retains the public MONA callback mechanism and key settings from the published notebook—<math id="S6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, entropy coefficient <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, clip range <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.3</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rate <math id="S6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\!\times\!10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\!\times\!10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>—while adding architectural improvements for research usability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>:</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="S6.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:1.3em;">
<li id="S6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A custom CNN feature extractor over channel-first 2D board observations, converting categorical grid states into spatial feature planes.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">SubprocVecEnv</span> with 4 parallel workers for rollout collection.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reward normalization via <span id="S6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">VecNormalize</span> (observation normalization off, reward normalization on) so PPO updates see normalized approval rewards.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A MONA callback that repacks vectorized rollouts into horizon-limited subepisodes, preserving timestep-level reward alignment (verified by an explicit test in the repository <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>).</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">These are deliberate divergences from the single-environment flat-observation public setup, documented in the repository’s fidelity notes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.
The extension should be understood as an improved experimental variant, not a bitwise replica.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.3 </span>Modular Approval Construction</h3>

<div id="S6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This is the conceptual core of the extension.
Instead of treating approval as a single exact tensor, the code supports a family of approval builders that can be swapped into the same training loop.
The learned-overseer path constructs the approval reward from two supervised models trained over trajectory-sampled <math id="S6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(t,s,a)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(t,s,a)</annotation></semantics></math> tuples: one predicting intended-behavior probability and one predicting hacked-behavior probability.
Their difference becomes the reward override:</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float">Listing 1: </span>Core logic of the learned-approval construction, from <span id="LST1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">approval_spectrum/overseers.py</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</figcaption>
<div id="LST1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7FA;--ltx-border-color:#C8C8D2;"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
<div id="lstnumberx1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1</span>
              
              
              
            <span id="lstnumberx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">dataset</span><span id="lstnumberx1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">=</span><span id="lstnumberx1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">build_trajectory_dataset</span><span id="lstnumberx1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">(</span><span id="lstnumberx1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">oracle</span><span id="lstnumberx1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">approval_config</span><span id="lstnumberx1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">.</span><span id="lstnumberx1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">dataset</span><span id="lstnumberx1.14" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">,</span><span id="lstnumberx1.15" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_space ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;"> </span><span id="lstnumberx1.16" class="ltx_text ltx_lst_identifier ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">seed</span><span id="lstnumberx1.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="font-size:80%;">)</span>
</div>
