</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="S6.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Conceptual approval-reward construction spectrum from Appendix B.3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.
Safer constructions (left) are more restrictive and less outcome-dependent; moving right toward achieved-outcome dependence degrades safety until MONA recreates ordinary RL (point 6).
The bracket indicates the region addressed by this extension: oracle MONA, noisy and misspecified oracles, and learned outcome classifiers.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">6.4 </span>Experiment Surface</h3>

<div id="S6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The learned-approval suite sweeps over a structured set of configurations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>: approval method (ordinary RL, oracle MONA, noisy oracle, misspecified oracle, learned outcome classifier, calibrated outcome classifier), optimization horizon (<math id="S6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\{\texttt{None},1,4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">None</mtext><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\{\texttt{None},1,4\}</annotation></semantics></math>), environment (public Camera Dropbox, harder variant), learned-overseer dataset size (512, 2048), calibration strategy (none, sigmoid, isotonic), and PPO budget (768, 1536, 3072 steps).
The full configuration space is defined in <span id="S6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">approval_spectrum/configs.py</span> and all configs are published for exact reruns <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F4" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S6.F4.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="86.1" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 533.47 86.1" width="533.47"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,86.1) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(54.14,0) translate(0,43.05)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F7F7F7;" fill="#F7F7F7" stroke-width="0.45pt"><path d="M 48.29 42.74 L -48.29 42.74 C -51.35 42.74 -53.82 40.26 -53.82 37.21 L -53.82 -37.21 C -53.82 -40.26 -51.35 -42.74 -48.29 -42.74 L 48.29 -42.74 C 51.35 -42.74 53.82 -40.26 53.82 -37.21 L 53.82 37.21 C 53.82 40.26 51.35 42.74 48.29 42.74 Z M -53.82 -42.74"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.45pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -49.21 30.44)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:8.36em;--ltx-fo-height:0.56em;--ltx-fo-depth:4.96em;font-size:10pt;" height="76.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 7.69)" width="115.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
