<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S6.F4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S6.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reproduction-first workflow.
The project starts from the public MONA Camera Dropbox release, repackages it as a Python project, adds modular learned-approval mechanisms, and evaluates safety–capability tradeoffs across the approval-construction space.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S7" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">7 </span>Pilot Results</h2>

<section id="S7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.1 </span>Public Reference: Confirming the Original Contrast</h3>

<div id="S7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The strongest result in this work is inherited from the original MONA artifact.
Using the released public PPO reference arrays <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, the canonical contrast is clear: the ordinary-RL reference finishes with a reward-hacking rate of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.915" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.915</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.915</annotation></semantics></math> and an intended-behavior rate of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.077" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.077</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.077</annotation></semantics></math>, whereas the oracle MONA reference finishes with a reward-hacking rate of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.000</annotation></semantics></math> and an intended-behavior rate of <math id="S7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.999</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.999</annotation></semantics></math>.
This matches the qualitative PPO result reported in the original paper: ordinary PPO learns camera-blocking and reward hacking, while MONA with oracle approval learns the intended single-box behavior <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">7.2 </span>Learned-Approval Pilot: Safety Without Capability</h3>

<div id="S7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The new empirical content is more modest but informative.
In the executed reduced-budget pilot sweeps, PPO did not re-enter the strong reward-hacking regime under any tested learned-approval configuration.
The dominant failure mode was under-optimization and persistent task failure <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S7.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S7.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The best reported learned-overseer run—a calibrated classifier on the public environment with horizon <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math>, sigmoid calibration, dataset size <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>512</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">512</annotation></semantics></math>, and a budget of <math id="S7.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1536" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1536</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1536</annotation></semantics></math> PPO steps—achieved:</p>
</div>
<figure id="S7.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S7.T2.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 2</span>: </span><span id="S7.T2.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Key metrics for the three main comparison points.
<em id="S7.T2.6.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Public ref.</em> values are from the released MONA arrays <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.
<em id="S7.T2.6.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Best learned</em> is the best calibrated learned-overseer run from the local pilot <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</span></figcaption>
